Hello,

I'm having an issue when formatting a ubifs to nand flash using 
ubiformat on the i.MX28.  It seems to pass the block checks but the 
kernel crashes when it attempts formats the first block.

I'm using the kernel Artem's from: 
http://git.infradead.org/users/dedekind/l2-mtd-2.6.git 
<http://git.infradead.org/users/dedekind/l2-mtd-2.6.git>
I applied Shawn Guo's DMA patchesfrom: 
http://git.infradead.org/users/vkoul/slave-dma.git/commit/a580b8c5429a624d120cd603e1498bf676e2b4da
and the Huang Shijie's GPMI-NAND patches from: 
http://article.gmane.org/gmane.linux.ports.arm.kernel/110600 
<http://article.gmane.org/gmane.linux.ports.arm.kernel/110600/match=gpmi>

my cmdline is: console=ttyAMA0,115200 
mtdparts=gpmi-nand:20m(boot),-(user) gpmi_debug_init  
ip=192.168.137.1::192.168.137.254:255.255.255.0::eth0: root=/dev/nfs 
nfsroot=192.168.137.254:/tftpboot/gnet_amp,v3,tcp noinitrd

I've attached the kernel oops output and my .config file.  If anyone has 
any insight I would appreciate it.

Thanks,

-Matt Burtch

