    Hello, <br>
    <br>
    I'm having an issue when formatting a ubifs to nand flash using
    ubiformat on the i.MX28.&nbsp; It seems to pass the block checks but the
    kernel crashes when it attempts formats the first block.<br>
    <br>
    I'm using the kernel Artem's from: <font size="3"><a
        href="http://git.infradead.org/users/dedekind/l2-mtd-2.6.git">http://git.infradead.org/users/dedekind/l2-mtd-2.6.git
      </a><br>
      I applied </font>Shawn Guo's DMA patches<font size="3"> from: </font><a
      class="moz-txt-link-freetext"
href="http://git.infradead.org/users/vkoul/slave-dma.git/commit/a580b8c5429a624d120cd603e1498bf676e2b4da">http://git.infradead.org/users/vkoul/slave-dma.git/commit/a580b8c5429a624d120cd603e1498bf676e2b4da</a><br>
    and the Huang Shijie's GPMI-NAND patches from: <a
href="http://article.gmane.org/gmane.linux.ports.arm.kernel/110600/match=gpmi">http://article.gmane.org/gmane.linux.ports.arm.kernel/110600</a><br>
    <br>
    my cmdline is: console=ttyAMA0,115200
    mtdparts=gpmi-nand:20m(boot),-(user) gpmi_debug_init&nbsp;
    ip=192.168.137.1::192.168.137.254:255.255.255.0::eth0: root=/dev/nfs
    nfsroot=192.168.137.254:/tftpboot/gnet_amp,v3,tcp noinitrd<br>
    <br>
    I've attached the kernel oops output and my .config file.&nbsp; If anyone
    has any insight I would appreciate it.<br>
    <br>
    Thanks,<br>
    <br>
    -Matt Burtch<br>
